pra: start the process sampler on the eMMC path, aim it at Setup

The hello screen never presents because Setup (com.apple.purplebuddy)
hangs at scene creation and the launch watchdog kills it (0x8badf00d,
20 s process-launch on the 0151 boots, 300 s scene-create since). Its
second thread parks in xpc_connection_send_message_with_reply_sync()
waiting for a reply that never comes; the 0153 probe was built to name
the peer, but in the 0160 boot its 128-entry table filled before the
smoking gun and the sampled overflow was dominated by a
kernel_task -> Setup id=0x0 flood that is not a real RPC.

- pra_sdhci now starts the SWEET process sampler where the root device
  becomes ready. The sampler's start was hooked into sweet_ufs, which
  never attaches on this eMMC phone, so sweetsample has been dead here
  since 0054 (0 "SMP" lines in ring17 despite the default boot-arg).
- pra_msg_probe: table 128 -> 512 triples, and messages with msgh_id 0
  are skipped entirely so the flood cannot fill the table again.
- sweet_sample: 90 samples every 120 s (was 40) - PRA boots run for
  hours and Setup is relaunched after each watchdog kill, so the
  sampler must outlive the first 300 s hang.

Boot with sweetsample=Setup: the sampler prints Setup's full user
pc/lr/sp plus fp backtraces ("SMP Setup[pid] slide ...") every 2
minutes through the hang, and the offline symbolication (research/ipsw-x
cache + .symbols, slide printed per sample) names the peer and the
message Setup is stuck on.
diff --git a/bsd/dev/pra_sdhci.c b/bsd/dev/pra_sdhci.c
--- a/bsd/dev/pra_sdhci.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/pra_sdhci.c
@@ -48,6 +48,7 @@
 #include <machine/atomic.h>
 
 extern vm_offset_t ml_io_map(vm_offset_t phys_addr, vm_size_t size);
+extern void sweet_sample_start(void); /* bsd/dev/sweet_sample.c */
 
 #define PRA_SDHCI_BASE_DEFAULT 0xFF390000ULL
 
@@ -1768,6 +1769,15 @@ pra_emmc_rootdev(dev_t *dev)
 		    pra_emmc_partition_name,
 		    pra_emmc_writable ? "writable" : "read-only");
 		pra_log_start();
+		/*
+		 * The SWEET process sampler (sweet_sample.c) is started from the
+		 * sweet_ufs probe, which never attaches on this eMMC phone - the
+		 * sweetsample boot-arg has been dead here since 0054. Start it
+		 * where the root device becomes ready: sweetsample=Setup is what
+		 * catches the com.apple.purplebuddy scene-create hang (the hello
+		 * screen blocker, 0x8badf00d kills since the 0151 boots).
+		 */
+		sweet_sample_start();
 	}
 	*dev = pra_emmc_bdev;
 	return 0;
diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_sample.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_sample.c
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_sample.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_sample.c
@@ -72,7 +72,10 @@ sweet_sample_thread(__unused void *arg, __unused wait_result_t wr)
 		return;
 	}
 	(void)tsleep(&chan, PZERO, "sweetsmp", 90 * hz);
-	for (int i = 0; i < 40; i++) {
+	/* 90 samples x 120 s: PRA boots run for hours and Setup is relaunched
+	 * after each 0x8badf00d kill, so the sampler must outlive the first
+	 * hang (300 s scene-create watchdog) and catch the later ones. */
+	for (int i = 0; i < 90; i++) {
 		printf("SMP --- sample %d\n", i);
 		proc_iterate(PROC_ALLPROCLIST, sweet_sample_proc, NULL, NULL, NULL);
 		(void)tsleep(&chan, PZERO, "sweetsmp", 120 * hz);
